Now rewrite the store. Let me design it.

Types:
- TicketStatus stays.
- Ticket gains: executionStatus?, clarification?, error?, traceId?, requestsSpent?, cleanup?, duplicate?.

New context value:
- tickets, inventory, fixtures, health, apiError
- refreshHealth, loadFixtures
- submitAgentTicket(input): Promise<Ticket>  (202 accepted)
- loadCase(id): Promise<AgentStatusOut | null>
- getTimeline(id): Promise<TimelineEvent[]>
- continueCase(id, input): Promise<AgentContinueOut>
- caseStatus: Record<string, AgentStatusOut>
- simulateTicket, submitCustomerTicket, resetMockData, getTicket

Polling:
- pollers ref Map<string, number>.
- watchCase(id): if pollers has id, return. tick: try getAgentCase → applyStatus; if status.execution_status is "queued" or "running", schedule setTimeout(tick, POLL_MS); else delete from map.
- cleanup on unmount.

applyStatus updates tickets + caseStatus.

Map status to view:
```
function statusView(status: AgentStatusOut): { status: TicketStatus; statusLabel: string; actions: string[] } {
  switch (status.execution_status) {
    case "queued": return { status: "processing", statusLabel: "Queued" };
    case "running": return { status: "processing", statusLabel: "Agent Processing" };
    case "waiting_input": return { status: "processing", statusLabel: "Clarification Required" };
    case "failed": return { status: "escalated", statusLabel: "Run Failed" };
    case "completed":
      if (status.outcome === "denial") return { status: "escalated", statusLabel: "Policy Denied" };
      if (status.outcome === "escalation") return { status: "escalated", statusLabel: "Escalated to Human" };
      if (status.outcome === "clarification") return { status: "processing", statusLabel: "Clarification Required" };
      return { status: "resolved", statusLabel: "Resolved Autonomously" };
  }
}
```

actions: from runs -> runs.map(r => r.toUpperCase()). Or keep simple ["INTAKE"] + runs. Let me set actions from status.runs: `status.runs.map((r) => r.toUpperCase())`; fall back to ["INTAKE"].

Actually the ticket "actions" display chips on dashboard; using run ids is fine but odd. Previously they were operation steps. With agent we don't get steps in status (only in timeline). I'll derive actions as ["INTAKE", ...status.runs] mapping. Hmm. Let me keep actions = status.runs.length ? status.runs.map(r => r.toUpperCase()) : ["INTAKE"]. Fine.

submitAgentTicket:
```
const accepted = await apiSubmitAgentTicket(input);
const ticket: Ticket = {
  id: accepted.case_id,
  message: input.message,
  status: "processing",
  statusLabel: accepted.execution_status === "queued" ? "Queued" : "Agent Processing",
  actions: ["INTAKE", accepted.run_id.toUpperCase()],
  time: "Just now",
  sku: input.order_item_id ?? "—",
  live: true,
  executionStatus: accepted.execution_status,
  runId: accepted.run_id,
  duplicate: accepted.duplicate,
};
rememberTicket(ticket);
setHealth("online"); setApiError(null);
startWatch(accepted.case_id);
return ticket;
```

loadCase(id):
```
try {
  const status = await apiGetAgentCase(id);
  applyStatus(id, status);
  if (active) startWatch(id);
  return status;
} catch { return null; }
```

getTimeline → apiGetAgentCaseTimeline.

continueCase(id, input):
```
const result = await apiContinueAgentCase(id, input);
if (result.continued) {
  setTickets map -> executionStatus "queued", status processing, statusLabel "Queued", reply null, error null
  startWatch(id);
} else {
  // terminal; refresh status once
  const status = await apiGetAgentCase(id); applyStatus(...) maybe
}
return result;
```

keep simpler: after continue, always startWatch(id) if continued, else call loadCase to refresh.

applyStatus also updates caseStatus map.

Need to guard setState after unmount? Pollers cleared on unmount. Fine, but a fetch may resolve after unmount; acceptable minor warning. Actually the eslint set-state-in-effect rule is about setState directly in effect; not this. Fine.

startWatch must be stable and reference itself. Use a ref pattern or useCallback with recursion via ref. Implement with a ref holding the tick function? Simplest: define `startWatch` as useCallback that uses a local recursive function:

```
const pollers = useRef(new Map<string, number>());
const watchCase = useCallback((id: string) => {
  if (pollers.current.has(id)) return;
  const poll = async () => {
    try {
      const status = await apiGetAgentCase(id);
      applyStatus(id, status);
      if (status.execution_status === "queued" || status.execution_status === "running") {
        const t = window.setTimeout(poll, POLL_MS);
        pollers.current.set(id, t);
      } else {
        pollers.current.delete(id);
      }
    } catch {
      pollers.current.delete(id);
    }
  };
  const t = window.setTimeout(poll, 0);
  pollers.current.set(id, t);
}, [applyStatus]);
```

But initial `pollers.current.set(id, t)` then inside poll it resets. Fine.

applyStatus as useCallback:
```
const applyStatus = useCallback((id, status) => {
  setCaseStatus((prev) => ({ ...prev, [id]: status }));
  const view = statusView(status);
  setTickets((prev) => prev.map((t) => t.id === id ? {
    ...t,
    status: view.status,
    statusLabel: view.statusLabel,
    actions: view.actions,
    outcome: status.outcome ?? undefined,
    reply: status.reply ?? undefined,
    exchangeId: status.exchange_id,
    executionStatus: status.execution_status,
    clarification: status.clarification,
    error: status.error,
    traceId: status.trace_id,
    requestsSpent: status.requests_spent,
    cleanup: status.cleanup,
    runId: status.current_run_id ?? t.runId,
  } : t));
}, []);
```

Unmount cleanup:
```
useEffect(() => () => {
  pollers.current.forEach((t) => window.clearTimeout(t));
  pollers.current.clear();
}, []);
```

watchCase depends on applyStatus which is stable.

Also start watching rehydrated live cases that are still active after mount? Optional. Could cause many polls. Skip; detail page loadCase will start watch.

Now `getCase` renamed to `loadCase`. Ticket detail uses it.

Let me also keep the offline fallbacks (simulateTicket, submitCustomerTicket) unchanged.

Remove armFault/clearFaults/submitTicket.

