```
const refreshCases = useCallback(async () => {
  try {
    const result = await apiListAgentCases({ limit: 25 });
    setApiError(null);
    if (result.items.length > 0) {
      setTickets((prev) => {
        const incoming = result.items.map(ticketFromCase);
        const incomingIds = new Set(incoming.map((t) => t.id));
        const keep = prev.filter((t) => !incomingIds.has(t.id) && !t.live);
        return [...incoming, ...keep];
      });
    }
    return result;
  } catch {
    return null;
  }
}, []);
```
Wait—this drops live session tickets not in incoming? `keep` filters out tickets whose id is in incoming and also filters out previous live tickets (since !t.live). If a session-created live ticket is in incoming (backend lists it), it's replaced by incoming version. Good. If a session live ticket is not yet in incoming (race), it'd be dropped because !t.live is false. Hmm. To be safe keep prev live tickets that aren't in incoming:
```
const keep = prev.filter((t) => !incomingIds.has(t.id) && (t.live || <seeded>));
```
But seeded mocks have live undefined (false) and id TCK-*. So `t.live || !t.id.startsWith("CASE-")`? Simplest: keep everything not in incoming:
```
const keep = prev.filter((t) => !incomingIds.has(t.id));
return [...incoming, ...keep];
```
This keeps mocks and session tickets not listed. Since backend cases have CASE- ids and mocks TCK-, no dupes. But incoming cases that were previously in prev get replaced. Good. This is simplest and safe.

So:
```
setTickets((prev) => {
  const incoming = result.items.map(ticketFromCase);
  const incomingIds = new Set(incoming.map((t) => t.id));
  return [...incoming, ...prev.filter((t) => !incomingIds.has(t.id))];
});
```

