Only one warning: the second eslint-disable directive in the mount effect is unused (because set-state-in-effect only flagged the first?). Actually the rule flags the whole effect; the second directive line is unused. Let me remove the second disable comment.

The mount effect:
```
    // eslint-disable-next-line react-hooks/set-state-in-effect
    void fetchPage("", null, false);
    // eslint-disable-next-line react-hooks/set-state-in-effect
    void refreshStatus();
```
Remove the second directive. But will the rule then flag refreshStatus? The rule flags setState calls in effects. `refreshStatus` calls setState inside a callback (async), not directly in effect body, so it may not be flagged. The lint output says no problems reported for the second directive, meaning the line after it (void refreshStatus()) didn't trigger the rule. So removing the directive is safe.

Let me remove it.

